{
  "title": "Mech Blocks Reference",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Every block Mech knows, as Mech Blocks understands it from reading Ward Cunningham's code in October 2026. The descriptions follow Ward's [[Catalog of Mech Blocks]]. How to use the tool is in the [[Mech Blocks Manual]].",
      "id": "0f278a7363cf2632"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "42e1f92e68202520",
      "text": "*Marc Pierson and Claude Opus 5.5 · October 2026*",
      "attribution": true
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "**Needs** is what a block reads from the shared state, which a block above it must make. **Makes** is what it writes there for blocks below. **Holds** is what may be indented under it.",
      "id": "d938235c27f93321"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Blocks that run in the browser",
      "id": "a40ffbfded3a99fb"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "text": "<table>\n<tr><th>Block</th><th>What it does</th><th>Needs</th><th>Makes</th><th>Holds</th></tr>\n<tr><td>CLICK</td><td>Offer to proceed once user clicks.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>blocks (must)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>TICK</td><td>Proceed repeatedly once user clicks.</td><td>—</td><td>🌡 tick, for the blocks inside</td><td>blocks (must)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>UNTIL</td><td>Stop TICKing once a word turns up.</td><td>🌡 tick; 🔗 aspect</td><td>—</td><td>blocks, if you like</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SLEEP</td><td>Suspend a sequence of blocks.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>blocks, if you like</td></tr>\n<tr><td>TOGETHER</td><td>Start all blocks at once.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>blocks (must)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>FROM</td><td>Fetch a page for the blocks indented below.</td><td>—</td><td>🏘 page</td><td>blocks (must)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>NEIGHBORS</td><td>Retrieve available neighborhood sitemaps.</td><td>—</td><td>🏘 neighborhood</td><td>lines of data</td></tr>\n<tr><td>WALK</td><td>Explore the neighborhood link graph.</td><td>🏘 neighborhood</td><td>🔗 aspect</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>RANDOM</td><td>Select a random page from the neighbors.</td><td>🏘 neighborhood</td><td>🏘 info</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>ROSTER</td><td>Make a Roster for the current neighborhood.</td><td>🏘 neighborhood</td><td>☰ items</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>LINEUP</td><td>Make a page from the current lineup.</td><td>—</td><td>☰ items</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SHOW</td><td>Add an existing page to the lineup. Shows a result.</td><td>🏘 info when no page is named</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DELTA</td><td>Apply recent remote site changes.</td><td>🖥 actions for apply</td><td>🖥 recent for have; 🏘 page for apply</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SOURCE</td><td>Read a data source from the lineup.</td><td>—</td><td>the topic named, such as 🔗 marker</td><td>blocks, if you like</td></tr>\n<tr><td>FILE</td><td>User selects one of the available files.</td><td>📄 assets</td><td>📄 the file text, named by the suffix as typed, for the blocks inside</td><td>blocks (must)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>KWIC</td><td>Construct a Keyword-In-Context index.</td><td>📄 tsv</td><td>☰ items</td><td>lines of data</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SENSOR</td><td>Read sensor data from a named endpoint.</td><td>🏘 page</td><td>🌡 temperature</td><td>blocks, if you like</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CODE</td><td>Run JavaScript from a Code item on this page.</td><td>—</td><td>◆ whatever its function sets</td><td>lines of data</td></tr>\n<tr><td>HELLO</td><td>Add a happy face each time run. Shows a result.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>REPORT</td><td>Report a measurement in place in the item. Shows a result.</td><td>🌡 temperature, or the key named after REPORT</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>PREVIEW</td><td>Display computed state as a ghost page. Shows a result.</td><td>🔗 marker for map; 🔗 aspect for graph; ☰ items for items; 🏘 page for page</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>POPUP</td><td>Open a pop-up window with various contents. Shows a result.</td><td>🖥 commons for images</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SOLO</td><td>Launch the Solo plugin pop-up viewer. Shows a result.</td><td>🔗 aspect</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>PRINT</td><td>Compose a printable story and garden. Shows a result.</td><td>🔗 aspect; 🏘 neighborhood</td><td>☰ items</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DOWNLOAD</td><td>Download state as a file. Shows a result.</td><td>📄 the state named by the file ending</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>GET</td><td>Await a result from the server.</td><td>—</td><td>🖥 result</td><td>server blocks (must)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>PLUGIN</td><td>Await a result from an installed plugin.</td><td>—</td><td>🖥 result</td><td>the plugin's blocks (must)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>LISTEN</td><td>Wait for a specific message.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>MESSAGE</td><td>Send a specific message.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>FORWARD</td><td>Move the drawing \"turtle\" forward.</td><td>—</td><td>✏️ turtle</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>TURN</td><td>Turn the drawing \"turtle\".</td><td>—</td><td>✏️ turtle</td><td>nothing</td></tr>\n</table>",
      "id": "8bbcae43aebb8333"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Blocks that run on the server, inside GET",
      "id": "9c580823528c9396"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "text": "<table>\n<tr><th>Block</th><th>What it does</th><th>Needs</th><th>Makes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>HELLO</td><td>Add a happy face each time run.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td>UPTIME</td><td>Report time the server has run.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SLEEP</td><td>Suspend a sequence of blocks.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td>COMMONS</td><td>Report image files and byte count.</td><td>—</td><td>🖥 commons</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DELTA</td><td>Retrieve recent site changes.</td><td>🖥 recent</td><td>🖥 actions</td></tr>\n</table>",
      "id": "4f91bb0c6d5e788a"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "GET sends only the state named after it to the server, such as `GET recent`. Whatever the server blocks make comes back for the blocks after GET.",
      "id": "b48f1258b290f34c"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Blocks that run inside PLUGIN rcn",
      "id": "0ce9ac54fdec9dfc"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "These come with the Mech Blocks plugin and read RCN data held on the same site.",
      "id": "3e9afdd5c52818cb"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "text": "<table>\n<tr><th>Block</th><th>What it does</th><th>Needs</th><th>Makes</th></tr>\n<tr><td>PROJECTIONS</td><td>List the Layer 1 folders on this site.</td><td>—</td><td>☰ items</td></tr>\n<tr><td>PROJECTION</td><td>A Layer 1 folder's graph, as an aspect; kinds after the name keep only those.</td><td>—</td><td>🔗 aspect</td></tr>\n<tr><td>BADGES</td><td>SODOTO badges on this site's pages: people and the skills they hold; words after it keep matching skills.</td><td>—</td><td>🔗 aspect; ☰ items</td></tr>\n<tr><td>HELLO</td><td>Proves the rcn plugin answers.</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n</table>",
      "id": "2617143a00cedbdd"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Notes",
      "id": "0295ea62682123e9"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "- A block that is missing what it needs stops with a ✖︎ and makes nothing, so blocks after it that needed its result stop too.\n- FILE stores the file's text under its argument exactly as typed. `FILE tsv` makes tsv, which KWIC and DOWNLOAD can use. `FILE .tsv` stores it under \".tsv\", which they cannot find.\n- CODE runs for anyone only when it sits directly inside CLICK or TICK. Elsewhere it runs only for the page owner.\n- [[CODE]] and [[DOWNLOAD]] had no handbook pages; pages for them were drafted in October 2026.",
      "id": "cf536f20e44a1f69"
    }
  ],
